node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.mnemon/
.pnpm-store/
.cache/

# Packaged release artifacts. `pnpm pack` writes dock-flash-<version>.tgz, which is
# renamed to dock-flash.tgz for the GitHub Release upload — the registry entry's
# tarball URL points at releases/latest/download/dock-flash.tgz. Both forms are
# ignored: a stale tarball sitting in the tree is how a release ships the previous
# build, and the file is reproducible from the commit any time it is needed.
dock-flash.tgz
dock-flash-*.tgz

# Scratch files. Ad-hoc repro pages, throwaway scripts and API responses written while
# verifying a change all use a leading underscore, and `git add -A` has twice swept them
# into a commit — once baking a scratch JSON into history. They are never part of the
# published plugin (`files` in package.json does not list them either), so the pattern is
# ignored rather than trusted to be deleted in time.
_*.py
_*.mjs
_*.json
_*.html
_*.png
_*.txt
# Scratch DIRECTORIES follow the same convention (`_probe/` held a throwaway DSH home and
# profile). The file patterns above do not match a directory, so name it explicitly.
_*/

# Local AI-assistant tooling — developer-machine state, not part of the
# published plugin. graphflow-out/ holds a SQLite graph database and
# .graphflow-cache/ an index cache; neither belongs in a public repo.
.claude/
.windsurfrules
GEMINI.md
CLAUDE.md
.graphflow-cache/
.graphflow/
graphflow-out/
pnpm-lock.yaml
